1
00:00:00,818 --> 00:00:03,804
On day 361, Vera walks the bridge.

2
00:00:03,804 --> 00:00:05,241
She does it alone,

3
00:00:05,241 --> 00:00:08,330
at first light, from one end to the other and back,

4
00:00:08,330 --> 00:00:10,888
in her long grey scarf, looking down.

5
00:00:11,326 --> 00:00:12,526
Not at the river.

6
00:00:12,526 --> 00:00:13,392
At the edge.

7
00:00:13,392 --> 00:00:15,679
At the place halfway across where

8
00:00:15,679 --> 00:00:16,983
the road just stops,

9
00:00:16,983 --> 00:00:20,439
and a long jagged bite of concrete has fallen into

10
00:00:20,439 --> 00:00:23,064
the brown water, and what is left

11
00:00:23,064 --> 00:00:25,841
beside it is barely wider than a coach.

12
00:00:26,263 --> 00:00:28,348
Your name is Patch.

13
00:00:28,348 --> 00:00:30,257
Three hundred and sixty days ago,

14
00:00:30,257 --> 00:00:32,411
you were waiting for a bus.

15
00:00:32,411 --> 00:00:35,212
Since then, you have lived under

16
00:00:35,212 --> 00:00:37,680
a bus depot, then above it on a hill,

17
00:00:38,294 --> 00:00:39,745
and then you gave the whole

18
00:00:39,745 --> 00:00:41,755
yard to the dead and drove away.

19
00:00:42,289 --> 00:00:44,591
Behind you, a sign over an

20
00:00:44,591 --> 00:00:47,193
empty street says SEVEN ALIVE.

21
00:00:47,679 --> 00:00:49,062
GONE TO THE SEA.

22
00:00:49,062 --> 00:00:52,500
In front of you, there is a broken bridge.

23
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:55,650
And somewhere past it, at the end of

24
00:00:55,650 --> 00:00:57,276
a beach on a postcard,

25
00:00:57,276 --> 00:01:00,197
thirty-one people are standing around a lighthouse,

26
00:01:00,197 --> 00:01:03,148
waiting for the lowest tide of the year.

27
00:01:03,148 --> 00:01:04,956
Vera comes back and stands in

28
00:01:04,956 --> 00:01:06,535
front of the coach with her

29
00:01:06,535 --> 00:01:08,173
hands in the ends of her scarf.

30
00:01:08,173 --> 00:01:10,310
"It's wide enough," she says.

31
00:01:10,310 --> 00:01:10,961
"Nearly."

32
00:01:10,961 --> 00:01:13,942
Bram looks up at the roof of the coach,

33
00:01:13,942 --> 00:01:15,087
where four sections of

34
00:01:15,087 --> 00:01:17,718
motorway barrier are strapped down tight.

35
00:01:17,718 --> 00:01:19,573
Then he looks at the gap.

36
00:01:19,573 --> 00:01:22,017
Then he whistles three notes.

37
00:01:22,017 --> 00:01:23,364
"Done," says Kit.

38
00:01:23,364 --> 00:01:25,948
"He means he's already done it.

39
00:01:25,948 --> 00:01:26,868
In his head."

40
00:01:26,868 --> 00:01:29,101
They lay the barrier sections

41
00:01:29,101 --> 00:01:30,598
along the broken edge,

42
00:01:30,598 --> 00:01:33,044
side by side, flat on the road,

43
00:01:33,044 --> 00:01:36,649
sticking out over the gap like the fingers of a hand.

44
00:01:36,649 --> 00:01:38,842
Then you weigh down the back ends.

45
00:01:39,297 --> 00:01:41,408
Bram sits on one by himself.

46
00:01:41,408 --> 00:01:43,883
You and Kit sit on the next.

47
00:01:43,883 --> 00:01:45,630
Ruth and Nora on the third.

48
00:01:45,630 --> 00:01:47,143
On the fourth,

49
00:01:47,143 --> 00:01:48,879
the spare wheel from the truck,

50
00:01:48,879 --> 00:01:52,297
and every loose stone you can carry from the riverbank.

51
00:01:52,297 --> 00:01:53,360
It gives the road one

52
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:54,723
more stripe of width.

53
00:01:55,256 --> 00:01:56,449
Not much.

54
00:01:56,449 --> 00:01:57,641
A stripe.

55
00:01:57,641 --> 00:02:00,307
Vera climbs into the driver's seat.

56
00:02:00,307 --> 00:02:02,872
Wes walks backward in front of the coach,

57
00:02:02,872 --> 00:02:04,185
holding up his little

58
00:02:04,185 --> 00:02:06,453
round mirror so she can see the edge.

59
00:02:06,453 --> 00:02:07,890
Nobody else breathes.

60
00:02:07,890 --> 00:02:09,633
The coach comes onto the bridge

61
00:02:09,633 --> 00:02:12,071
at the speed of a very slow queue.

62
00:02:12,071 --> 00:02:13,194
At the broken place,

63
00:02:13,194 --> 00:02:15,392
the right-hand wheels roll off the

64
00:02:15,392 --> 00:02:17,349
concrete and onto the barrier.

65
00:02:17,349 --> 00:02:19,016
The metal groans.

66
00:02:19,016 --> 00:02:20,546
It bends, just a little,

67
00:02:20,546 --> 00:02:23,172
under the weight, out over the water.

68
00:02:23,579 --> 00:02:24,708
You feel it through

69
00:02:24,708 --> 00:02:26,233
the seat of your trousers.

70
00:02:26,233 --> 00:02:29,466
And Vera turns the big wheel with two fingers,

71
00:02:29,466 --> 00:02:30,647
like a teacup,

72
00:02:30,647 --> 00:02:34,377
and keeps going, and doesn't look down once.

73
00:02:34,377 --> 00:02:37,210
Then the wheels are back on concrete.

74
00:02:37,210 --> 00:02:38,869
The coach is across.

75
00:02:38,869 --> 00:02:40,427
Then it's your turn.

76
00:02:40,427 --> 00:02:42,940
The truck is narrower than the coach.

77
00:02:43,586 --> 00:02:45,437
It doesn't need the barrier.

78
00:02:45,437 --> 00:02:47,337
It only needs somebody who

79
00:02:47,337 --> 00:02:49,097
doesn't look at the water.

80
00:02:49,097 --> 00:02:50,597
You climb into the cab,

81
00:02:50,597 --> 00:02:52,765
and Nora climbs in beside you,

82
00:02:52,765 --> 00:02:54,582
with the turquoise bag on her knees,

83
00:02:54,582 --> 00:02:56,863
and she doesn't say anything at all.

84
00:02:56,863 --> 00:02:58,521
Wes walks backward in front of you

85
00:02:58,521 --> 00:03:01,008
with the mirror, the way he did for Vera.

86
00:03:01,008 --> 00:03:02,192
At the broken place,

87
00:03:02,192 --> 00:03:04,327
you can see the river through the gap

88
00:03:04,327 --> 00:03:06,002
out of the corner of your eye.

89
00:03:06,002 --> 00:03:06,680
Brown.

90
00:03:07,198 --> 00:03:07,764
Fast.

91
00:03:07,764 --> 00:03:09,180
Very far down.

92
00:03:09,180 --> 00:03:11,186
You don't look at it.

93
00:03:11,186 --> 00:03:12,388
You look at Wes,

94
00:03:12,388 --> 00:03:16,039
and at his mirror, and at his free hand going left,

95
00:03:16,039 --> 00:03:17,612
left, straight, straight.

96
00:03:17,953 --> 00:03:19,259
Then concrete.

97
00:03:19,259 --> 00:03:20,826
Then the far end.

98
00:03:20,826 --> 00:03:24,088
Then Vera, standing beside the coach,

99
00:03:24,088 --> 00:03:27,920
nodding once, the way she nods at a good bus.

100
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:29,736
Nora lets go of the bag.

101
00:03:29,736 --> 00:03:32,234
You notice she has been holding it so

102
00:03:32,234 --> 00:03:34,265
hard that her fingers have gone white.

103
00:03:34,688 --> 00:03:35,432
Bram gets up,

104
00:03:35,432 --> 00:03:37,505
picks up the first section of barrier,

105
00:03:37,505 --> 00:03:39,938
and carries it back to the roof.

106
00:03:39,938 --> 00:03:42,765
"In case anything needs a gate," says Wes.

107
00:03:43,365 --> 00:03:44,168
"I know.

108
00:03:44,168 --> 00:03:45,272
I know."

109
00:03:46,418 --> 00:03:49,466
On day 362, you see the sea.

110
00:03:49,953 --> 00:03:52,084
You come over the last low hill at midday,

111
00:03:52,084 --> 00:03:53,906
the truck behind the coach,

112
00:03:53,906 --> 00:03:56,538
and suddenly there is no more land.

113
00:03:56,538 --> 00:03:58,807
Just a long pale beach,

114
00:03:58,807 --> 00:04:01,758
curving away, and beyond it the sea,

115
00:04:02,197 --> 00:04:04,306
enormous and flat and shining,

116
00:04:04,306 --> 00:04:07,188
all the way to the edge of the sky.

117
00:04:07,188 --> 00:04:08,436
You stop the truck.

118
00:04:08,436 --> 00:04:10,046
You don't decide to.

119
00:04:10,436 --> 00:04:11,707
Your foot does it.

120
00:04:11,707 --> 00:04:14,013
Nora gets out without a word.

121
00:04:14,387 --> 00:04:15,627
She stands at the side of the

122
00:04:15,627 --> 00:04:16,784
road with the turquoise bag

123
00:04:16,784 --> 00:04:18,995
hanging from one hand, and she looks.

124
00:04:18,995 --> 00:04:21,376
Then she takes the postcard

125
00:04:21,376 --> 00:04:22,756
out of her bag, holds it up in

126
00:04:22,756 --> 00:04:24,613
front of her, and lowers it again.

127
00:04:25,149 --> 00:04:26,183
It's the same.

128
00:04:26,183 --> 00:04:27,838
The long curve of sand.

129
00:04:27,838 --> 00:04:30,468
And at the far end of the beach,

130
00:04:30,468 --> 00:04:33,150
out in the water, a dark rock with little

131
00:04:33,150 --> 00:04:35,498
houses on it, and a white lighthouse.

132
00:04:35,807 --> 00:04:36,593
The Point.

133
00:04:36,593 --> 00:04:38,522
And then you see the rest.

134
00:04:38,522 --> 00:04:39,785
The road to it,

135
00:04:39,785 --> 00:04:42,258
the long, low causeway of stone,

136
00:04:42,258 --> 00:04:45,735
runs out across the sand from the end of the beach.

137
00:04:45,735 --> 00:04:46,796
The tide is half in,

138
00:04:46,796 --> 00:04:48,783
and the causeway is half covered.

139
00:04:48,783 --> 00:04:50,068
And along it,

140
00:04:50,068 --> 00:04:52,525
standing up to their knees in the sea,

141
00:04:52,525 --> 00:04:55,007
to their waists, to their chests,

142
00:04:55,007 --> 00:04:58,384
all the way out to the rock, stand the dead.

143
00:04:58,384 --> 00:05:00,266
A long dark line of them,

144
00:05:00,266 --> 00:05:02,162
facing the lighthouse.

145
00:05:02,162 --> 00:05:04,510
On the beach behind them, hundreds more.

146
00:05:04,981 --> 00:05:06,575
Waiting for the sea to go out.

147
00:05:06,575 --> 00:05:08,369
At the end of the causeway,

148
00:05:08,369 --> 00:05:11,096
where a gate should be, there is nothing at all.

149
00:05:11,096 --> 00:05:12,574
"They're on the rock?"

150
00:05:12,574 --> 00:05:14,076
says Wes quietly.

151
00:05:14,076 --> 00:05:15,460
"All of them?"

152
00:05:15,979 --> 00:05:18,516
"All of us," says Ruth.

153
00:05:18,516 --> 00:05:19,833
On day 362,

154
00:05:19,833 --> 00:05:22,340
after dark, Ruth knocks on the lighthouse.

155
00:05:22,340 --> 00:05:24,681
There is no other way to call.

156
00:05:24,681 --> 00:05:26,047
The radio only hisses

157
00:05:26,047 --> 00:05:27,776
this close to the sea.

158
00:05:28,295 --> 00:05:30,479
So Ruth takes the flashlight from

159
00:05:30,479 --> 00:05:33,107
Nora and stands on the roof of the coach,

160
00:05:33,107 --> 00:05:35,506
and points it across the dark

161
00:05:35,506 --> 00:05:38,206
water at the white tower, and flashes it.

162
00:05:38,206 --> 00:05:38,967
Twice.

163
00:05:39,277 --> 00:05:39,781
Hard.

164
00:05:39,781 --> 00:05:42,853
Nothing happens for a long time.

165
00:05:43,516 --> 00:05:45,610
Then, at the top of the lighthouse,

166
00:05:45,610 --> 00:05:47,365
the great lamp comes on.

167
00:05:47,787 --> 00:05:49,015
It doesn't turn.

168
00:05:49,015 --> 00:05:50,533
It just flashes,

169
00:05:50,533 --> 00:05:53,110
slowly, straight at you.

170
00:05:53,110 --> 00:05:54,028
Once.

171
00:05:54,467 --> 00:05:54,956
Twice.

172
00:05:54,956 --> 00:05:56,840
Kit makes a sound you have

173
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:59,037
never heard a person make.

174
00:05:59,037 --> 00:06:01,271
Ruth hands the flashlight back to Nora,

175
00:06:01,271 --> 00:06:03,417
and sits down on the roof of the coach,

176
00:06:03,417 --> 00:06:05,396
and puts her face in her hands.

177
00:06:05,915 --> 00:06:08,835
On day 363, a boat comes for you.

178
00:06:08,835 --> 00:06:10,702
It comes at high tide,

179
00:06:10,702 --> 00:06:12,569
when the causeway is under the sea and the

180
00:06:12,569 --> 00:06:14,309
dead have been pushed back up onto

181
00:06:14,309 --> 00:06:16,395
the beach in a long, dripping crowd.

182
00:06:16,929 --> 00:06:18,338
A small wooden fishing boat,

183
00:06:18,338 --> 00:06:20,686
rowed around the far side of the rock,

184
00:06:20,686 --> 00:06:22,460
all the way along the coast,

185
00:06:22,460 --> 00:06:25,971
to a little stone slipway at the other end of the beach,

186
00:06:25,971 --> 00:06:27,606
where none of the dead are standing.

187
00:06:27,606 --> 00:06:29,168
The man at the oars wears a

188
00:06:29,168 --> 00:06:30,794
dark green oilskin coat and

189
00:06:30,794 --> 00:06:33,011
a dark green fisherman's hat.

190
00:06:33,011 --> 00:06:34,868
When the boat touches the slipway,

191
00:06:34,868 --> 00:06:38,129
Kit is already in the water up to his knees.

192
00:06:38,129 --> 00:06:38,870
"Dad."

193
00:06:39,806 --> 00:06:42,503
Tam doesn't say anything for a long time.

194
00:06:42,503 --> 00:06:45,030
He just holds on to both of them,

195
00:06:45,030 --> 00:06:47,575
Kit and Ruth, in the shallow water,

196
00:06:47,575 --> 00:06:50,089
while the boat bumps against the stones.

197
00:06:50,089 --> 00:06:51,985
Bram stands on the slipway with

198
00:06:51,985 --> 00:06:53,818
his blanket around his shoulders,

199
00:06:53,818 --> 00:06:56,763
and whistles three notes, very softly.

200
00:06:56,763 --> 00:06:59,858
Then Tam looks up at the rest of you.

201
00:06:59,858 --> 00:07:00,594
The coach.

202
00:07:00,594 --> 00:07:01,629
The truck.

203
00:07:02,116 --> 00:07:03,831
A man in a red beanie.

204
00:07:03,831 --> 00:07:05,995
A woman in a grey scarf.

205
00:07:06,530 --> 00:07:07,936
A girl with a purple

206
00:07:07,936 --> 00:07:09,976
band and a turquoise bag.

207
00:07:10,366 --> 00:07:11,205
And you.

208
00:07:11,205 --> 00:07:14,021
"You're the depot," he says.

209
00:07:14,716 --> 00:07:16,942
"We're the depot," says Nora.

210
00:07:18,071 --> 00:07:22,271
From day 363 to day 364,

211
00:07:22,581 --> 00:07:25,241
Tam tells you about the door that opens once a year.

212
00:07:25,615 --> 00:07:27,016
He draws it for you in the wet

213
00:07:27,016 --> 00:07:29,146
sand of the slipway, with an oar.

214
00:07:29,146 --> 00:07:30,023
The beach.

215
00:07:30,023 --> 00:07:31,140
The causeway.

216
00:07:31,140 --> 00:07:31,937
The rock.

217
00:07:31,937 --> 00:07:34,212
And then, across the bay,

218
00:07:34,212 --> 00:07:36,497
on the other side, something else.

219
00:07:36,497 --> 00:07:38,748
A long, low tongue of sand running out

220
00:07:38,748 --> 00:07:41,711
from the beach into the sea, to a small hump

221
00:07:41,711 --> 00:07:44,383
of an island with an old stone fort on it.

222
00:07:44,383 --> 00:07:45,690
Nobody lives there.

223
00:07:45,690 --> 00:07:46,801
Nobody has lived

224
00:07:46,801 --> 00:07:48,430
there for a hundred years.

225
00:07:48,430 --> 00:07:51,016
"The Hump," says Tam.

226
00:07:51,016 --> 00:07:53,208
"You can only walk to it once a year.

227
00:07:53,208 --> 00:07:55,810
At the spring tide, the sea goes out

228
00:07:55,810 --> 00:07:57,994
so far that the sandbar comes up dry.

229
00:07:57,994 --> 00:08:00,614
For a few hours, you can walk across.

230
00:08:00,614 --> 00:08:02,045
Then the sea comes back.

231
00:08:02,045 --> 00:08:03,772
And it doesn't go out that

232
00:08:03,772 --> 00:08:05,625
far again until next spring."

233
00:08:05,625 --> 00:08:08,213
You look at the drawing for a long time.

234
00:08:08,213 --> 00:08:09,372
So does Vera.

235
00:08:09,970 --> 00:08:12,396
"A place with one way in," she says.

236
00:08:12,396 --> 00:08:14,631
"And the sea for a gate.

237
00:08:14,631 --> 00:08:15,605
For a year."

238
00:08:15,605 --> 00:08:18,040
"My favorite kind," says Nora,

239
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:19,385
before Vera can.

240
00:08:19,385 --> 00:08:20,888
Vera looks at her.

241
00:08:20,888 --> 00:08:22,688
And she smiles.

242
00:08:22,688 --> 00:08:23,689
A real one.

243
00:08:23,689 --> 00:08:26,755
The second you have ever seen.

244
00:08:26,755 --> 00:08:30,165
The plan takes all of day 364,

245
00:08:30,165 --> 00:08:34,805
and it is a plan you know by heart,

246
00:08:34,805 --> 00:08:37,313
because you have done it before.

247
00:08:37,313 --> 00:08:40,830
Only this time, the gate is the sea.

248
00:08:41,654 --> 00:08:42,938
At the lowest water,

249
00:08:42,938 --> 00:08:45,284
Vera will drive the coach down onto

250
00:08:45,284 --> 00:08:47,397
the hard wet sand, with the horn.

251
00:08:47,915 --> 00:08:49,574
Tam says the sand will hold;

252
00:08:49,574 --> 00:08:52,172
the fishermen used to drive tractors on it.

253
00:08:52,172 --> 00:08:53,826
The dead will come off the

254
00:08:53,826 --> 00:08:56,102
causeway and the beach toward the horn,

255
00:08:56,102 --> 00:08:57,625
the way they always do.

256
00:08:58,095 --> 00:09:00,217
Vera will lead them across the bay,

257
00:09:00,217 --> 00:09:02,522
along the sandbar, onto the Hump.

258
00:09:02,832 --> 00:09:04,661
Wes will tape the horn down.

259
00:09:04,661 --> 00:09:06,822
And then Vera and Wes will go out

260
00:09:06,822 --> 00:09:08,339
through the roof hatch,

261
00:09:08,339 --> 00:09:12,066
across the island, and down to the rocks on the far side,

262
00:09:12,066 --> 00:09:14,291
where Tam will be waiting with the boat.

263
00:09:15,196 --> 00:09:17,326
"Second door," says Wes.

264
00:09:18,117 --> 00:09:20,505
"Second door," says Vera.

265
00:09:21,698 --> 00:09:23,651
You and Nora will be in the truck at the

266
00:09:23,651 --> 00:09:26,182
top of the beach, to turn the stragglers

267
00:09:26,182 --> 00:09:28,447
who never follow anything the first time.

268
00:09:28,447 --> 00:09:30,446
And Bram, with the Point people,

269
00:09:30,446 --> 00:09:32,856
will carry four sections of motorway barrier

270
00:09:32,856 --> 00:09:35,060
across the rock to the end of the causeway.

271
00:09:35,060 --> 00:09:37,206
In case anything needs a gate.

272
00:09:37,206 --> 00:09:39,277
On day 365, the sea goes out.

273
00:09:39,277 --> 00:09:41,754
You have never seen anything like it.

274
00:09:41,754 --> 00:09:43,520
All morning, the water slides away

275
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:44,656
from the beach,

276
00:09:44,656 --> 00:09:47,806
farther and farther, until the whole bay is a shining

277
00:09:47,806 --> 00:09:49,026
plain of wet sand,

278
00:09:49,026 --> 00:09:51,426
and the causeway stands up out of it,

279
00:09:51,426 --> 00:09:54,686
dry from end to end, for the first time in a year.

280
00:09:55,334 --> 00:09:56,540
Out across the bay,

281
00:09:56,540 --> 00:09:59,465
a long pale back of sand rises out of the water

282
00:09:59,465 --> 00:10:01,853
and runs all the way to the Hump.

283
00:10:01,853 --> 00:10:04,475
And the dead walk out along the causeway,

284
00:10:04,475 --> 00:10:05,765
toward the rock.

285
00:10:06,092 --> 00:10:07,660
Hundreds of them.

286
00:10:07,660 --> 00:10:08,357
Slowly.

287
00:10:08,357 --> 00:10:09,789
All of them.

288
00:10:11,132 --> 00:10:13,267
On the rock, at the end of the causeway,

289
00:10:13,267 --> 00:10:14,621
Bram and the Point people

290
00:10:14,621 --> 00:10:17,042
bolt the four sections of barrier together,

291
00:10:17,042 --> 00:10:18,046
end to end,

292
00:10:18,410 --> 00:10:21,626
waist-high, from one side of the road to the other.

293
00:10:22,217 --> 00:10:23,667
The first of the dead reach it

294
00:10:23,667 --> 00:10:25,417
just as the last bolt goes in.

295
00:10:25,956 --> 00:10:26,658
They stop.

296
00:10:26,658 --> 00:10:28,445
They put their hands on it.

297
00:10:28,445 --> 00:10:29,957
They do not climb.

298
00:10:30,335 --> 00:10:31,951
It's the second gate you have ever

299
00:10:31,951 --> 00:10:34,781
closed with everyone on the right side of it.

300
00:10:34,781 --> 00:10:35,953
On day 365,

301
00:10:35,953 --> 00:10:38,991
Vera drives the coach onto the sand.

302
00:10:38,991 --> 00:10:40,502
You watch from the truck at

303
00:10:40,502 --> 00:10:41,795
the top of the beach,

304
00:10:41,795 --> 00:10:44,392
with Nora beside you and the engine running.

305
00:10:44,392 --> 00:10:46,690
The coach rolls down the slipway and

306
00:10:46,690 --> 00:10:48,129
out onto the wet sand,

307
00:10:48,129 --> 00:10:51,878
beige and patient, with the depot's name down its side and

308
00:10:51,878 --> 00:10:54,067
Wes in the seat beside Vera,

309
00:10:54,067 --> 00:10:57,063
and its wheels leave two long dark lines behind it.

310
00:10:57,063 --> 00:10:58,380
Then the horn.

311
00:10:58,380 --> 00:10:59,346
Not short.

312
00:10:59,346 --> 00:11:00,472
Long.

313
00:11:00,472 --> 00:11:03,531
The one that empties a flyover.

314
00:11:03,531 --> 00:11:06,187
It rolls out across the whole bay,

315
00:11:06,187 --> 00:11:09,048
and the long dark line on the causeway turns at once,

316
00:11:09,048 --> 00:11:11,324
like a field of wheat in the wind.

317
00:11:11,324 --> 00:11:13,187
They come down off the

318
00:11:13,187 --> 00:11:15,021
causeway onto the sand.

319
00:11:15,021 --> 00:11:15,933
Slowly.

320
00:11:16,394 --> 00:11:17,681
Then all of them.

321
00:11:17,681 --> 00:11:18,825
From the beach,

322
00:11:18,825 --> 00:11:22,158
from the causeway, from the edge of the water,

323
00:11:22,158 --> 00:11:25,012
hundreds of the dead walking out across the

324
00:11:25,012 --> 00:11:27,618
shining flats toward one beige bus.

325
00:11:27,618 --> 00:11:29,545
A few on the beach don't move.

326
00:11:29,545 --> 00:11:30,656
The ones who never

327
00:11:30,656 --> 00:11:32,734
follow anything the first time.

328
00:11:32,734 --> 00:11:34,852
You give them a second time.

329
00:11:34,852 --> 00:11:36,790
One blast of the truck's horn,

330
00:11:36,790 --> 00:11:37,833
and then another,

331
00:11:37,833 --> 00:11:41,177
and they turn toward you, and then toward the bigger

332
00:11:41,177 --> 00:11:43,413
sound out on the sand, and they go.

333
00:11:43,820 --> 00:11:45,493
The coach crawls across the bay,

334
00:11:45,493 --> 00:11:47,192
horn every few minutes,

335
00:11:47,192 --> 00:11:49,118
the dead strung out behind it in a line

336
00:11:49,118 --> 00:11:51,029
that runs back almost to the beach.

337
00:11:51,029 --> 00:11:52,294
Along the sandbar.

338
00:11:52,294 --> 00:11:53,993
Out toward the Hump.

339
00:11:54,414 --> 00:11:56,389
And everywhere around them,

340
00:11:56,389 --> 00:12:00,568
very quietly, the sea is starting to come back.

341
00:12:00,568 --> 00:12:02,720
On day 365, the tide turns.

342
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:05,519
You can see it from the top of the beach.

343
00:12:05,519 --> 00:12:07,342
A thin bright line of water

344
00:12:07,342 --> 00:12:09,126
creeping in from the edges of the bay,

345
00:12:09,126 --> 00:12:10,653
filling the low places first,

346
00:12:10,653 --> 00:12:13,021
wrapping around the end of the sandbar.

347
00:12:13,410 --> 00:12:14,955
The coach reaches the Hump and

348
00:12:14,955 --> 00:12:17,476
grinds up a slope of pebbles onto the island,

349
00:12:17,476 --> 00:12:19,425
right up beside the old fort.

350
00:12:19,425 --> 00:12:22,500
The dead follow it up out of the wet sand,

351
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:24,491
onto the island, around the coach.

352
00:12:24,491 --> 00:12:26,190
The horn goes on and on.

353
00:12:26,190 --> 00:12:27,789
Wes has taped it.

354
00:12:28,323 --> 00:12:29,074
Neatly.

355
00:12:29,074 --> 00:12:30,295
Very neatly.

356
00:12:30,295 --> 00:12:32,732
Then the roof hatch opens.

357
00:12:32,732 --> 00:12:34,358
Vera climbs out first,

358
00:12:34,358 --> 00:12:38,145
and Wes after her, and they run across the roof and drop

359
00:12:38,145 --> 00:12:39,695
down on the far side,

360
00:12:39,695 --> 00:12:42,008
and across the island, past the fort,

361
00:12:42,008 --> 00:12:45,816
down toward the rocks, where a small wooden boat is bobbing in

362
00:12:45,816 --> 00:12:48,617
the water that wasn't there an hour ago.

363
00:12:48,617 --> 00:12:51,034
Behind them, the last of the

364
00:12:51,034 --> 00:12:53,895
dead are still coming up off the sandbar,

365
00:12:53,895 --> 00:12:55,131
onto the island.

366
00:12:55,131 --> 00:12:56,076
Behind them,

367
00:12:56,076 --> 00:12:59,780
the sea is closing the sandbar like a zip.

368
00:12:59,780 --> 00:13:01,918
Wes slips on the rocks.

369
00:13:02,485 --> 00:13:03,930
His little round mirror flies

370
00:13:03,930 --> 00:13:04,846
out of his pocket,

371
00:13:04,846 --> 00:13:07,832
flashes once in the sun, and drops into the sea.

372
00:13:07,832 --> 00:13:09,566
He doesn't even look.

373
00:13:09,566 --> 00:13:10,669
Tam grabs his arm.

374
00:13:10,669 --> 00:13:12,352
Vera is already in the boat,

375
00:13:12,352 --> 00:13:14,259
holding out both hands.

376
00:13:14,259 --> 00:13:15,941
Wes falls in on top of her.

377
00:13:15,941 --> 00:13:17,838
Tam pulls on the oars.

378
00:13:17,838 --> 00:13:20,663
And behind them, the sea finishes closing.

379
00:13:20,663 --> 00:13:22,661
You stand on the top of the

380
00:13:22,661 --> 00:13:23,950
beach with Nora and watch the

381
00:13:23,950 --> 00:13:25,496
Hump become an island again.

382
00:13:26,031 --> 00:13:26,994
Around the coach,

383
00:13:26,994 --> 00:13:29,727
hundreds of the dead stand on the pebbles,

384
00:13:29,727 --> 00:13:32,374
facing a bus with a horn that is going to

385
00:13:32,374 --> 00:13:35,158
stop tonight and never blast again.

386
00:13:35,158 --> 00:13:36,507
And all around them,

387
00:13:36,507 --> 00:13:38,542
for a whole year, the sea.

388
00:13:39,206 --> 00:13:40,513
Nora doesn't say anything.

389
00:13:40,513 --> 00:13:42,797
She just puts her hand on your shoulder.

390
00:13:43,203 --> 00:13:44,024
Three times.

391
00:13:44,024 --> 00:13:46,969
And then a fourth time, softer.

392
00:13:47,535 --> 00:13:51,563
From day 366 to day 375,

393
00:13:51,563 --> 00:13:53,066
you live on the rock.

394
00:13:53,066 --> 00:13:54,433
The Point is small.

395
00:13:54,433 --> 00:13:57,235
One crooked street of stone houses,

396
00:13:57,235 --> 00:13:59,168
a harbor with six boats,

397
00:13:59,168 --> 00:14:00,889
nets drying on every wall,

398
00:14:00,889 --> 00:14:03,865
and gulls that are not afraid of anybody.

399
00:14:04,624 --> 00:14:05,672
The thirty-one of them make

400
00:14:05,672 --> 00:14:06,824
room for seven more as if

401
00:14:06,824 --> 00:14:08,611
they had been keeping it ready.

402
00:14:08,611 --> 00:14:10,543
Wes takes the cardboard with the

403
00:14:10,543 --> 00:14:12,007
totals out of his pocket,

404
00:14:12,007 --> 00:14:15,606
and adds thirty-one marks to people met, one at a time,

405
00:14:15,606 --> 00:14:18,291
very slowly, enjoying every single one.

406
00:14:18,291 --> 00:14:20,574
Then he gives the pencil to Tam,

407
00:14:20,574 --> 00:14:22,835
who adds five marks to his own wall,

408
00:14:22,835 --> 00:14:24,951
in the lighthouse, and then,

409
00:14:24,951 --> 00:14:28,291
after a while, two more, pressing very hard,

410
00:14:28,291 --> 00:14:31,477
with a fisherman's knot drawn next to them.

411
00:14:31,477 --> 00:14:34,148
On day 368, Bram oils the new

412
00:14:34,148 --> 00:14:36,670
gate at the end of the causeway,

413
00:14:36,670 --> 00:14:37,910
and whistles three notes,

414
00:14:37,910 --> 00:14:41,066
and goes to sleep against it, sitting up.

415
00:14:41,066 --> 00:14:43,534
Vera sleeps lying down,

416
00:14:43,534 --> 00:14:46,235
every night, with the door open.

417
00:14:46,235 --> 00:14:48,770
From day 376 to day 380,

418
00:14:48,770 --> 00:14:51,696
Nora goes to the beach.

419
00:14:51,696 --> 00:14:53,071
She waits for low tide.

420
00:14:53,071 --> 00:14:55,611
Then she walks out along the causeway,

421
00:14:55,611 --> 00:14:56,750
through Bram's gate,

422
00:14:56,750 --> 00:15:00,492
and onto the sand, and down to where the waves are coming in,

423
00:15:00,492 --> 00:15:01,934
and stands in the sea up to

424
00:15:01,934 --> 00:15:04,187
her ankles in her old cleaning shoes.

425
00:15:04,187 --> 00:15:06,138
You stand behind her.

426
00:15:06,138 --> 00:15:07,709
Wes stands behind you.

427
00:15:07,709 --> 00:15:09,429
The beach is empty.

428
00:15:09,429 --> 00:15:10,629
Not one of the dead,

429
00:15:10,629 --> 00:15:12,249
from one end to the other.

430
00:15:12,249 --> 00:15:14,453
Just sand, and wind, and gulls.

431
00:15:14,453 --> 00:15:16,841
"That's the beach," says Wes.

432
00:15:17,199 --> 00:15:18,092
"I promised."

433
00:15:18,092 --> 00:15:20,550
He takes his red beanie off.

434
00:15:21,213 --> 00:15:22,020
Fourth time.

435
00:15:22,020 --> 00:15:24,804
Nora takes the postcard out of her bag.

436
00:15:25,162 --> 00:15:25,957
Blue sea.

437
00:15:25,957 --> 00:15:26,991
Yellow sand.

438
00:15:26,991 --> 00:15:28,882
A white lighthouse.

439
00:15:29,481 --> 00:15:30,192
On the back,

440
00:15:30,192 --> 00:15:32,491
for the first time, she writes something,

441
00:15:32,491 --> 00:15:35,104
with Wes's pencil, leaning on your back.

442
00:15:35,104 --> 00:15:36,958
Then she gives it to you.

443
00:15:36,958 --> 00:15:38,663
It says: Still here.

444
00:15:38,663 --> 00:15:41,081
You put it in the orange bag,

445
00:15:41,081 --> 00:15:44,637
very carefully, next to Vera's goggles,

446
00:15:44,637 --> 00:15:47,777
next to everything else you are keeping.

447
00:15:47,777 --> 00:15:50,845
From day 381 to day 389,

448
00:15:50,845 --> 00:15:54,639
the door opens and closes by itself.

449
00:15:54,639 --> 00:15:57,010
Twice a day, the sea comes in and

450
00:15:57,010 --> 00:15:58,346
covers the causeway,

451
00:15:58,346 --> 00:16:01,408
and for six hours, nothing can walk to the Point.

452
00:16:01,408 --> 00:16:02,165
Twice a day,

453
00:16:02,165 --> 00:16:05,179
the sea goes out again, and the road comes back,

454
00:16:05,179 --> 00:16:06,873
and nobody comes down it.

455
00:16:06,873 --> 00:16:08,247
You learn the tides the

456
00:16:08,247 --> 00:16:09,500
way you learned the dead.

457
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:10,571
When they come.

458
00:16:10,961 --> 00:16:12,089
Where they stop.

459
00:16:12,089 --> 00:16:14,212
You never have to close a gate.

460
00:16:14,212 --> 00:16:16,184
The sea does it for you.

461
00:16:16,184 --> 00:16:16,931
Every sunset,

462
00:16:16,931 --> 00:16:19,648
Nora goes up the lighthouse with the radio,

463
00:16:19,648 --> 00:16:21,543
and says Still here into it.

464
00:16:21,543 --> 00:16:24,312
Most nights, nothing comes back.

465
00:16:24,312 --> 00:16:25,413
But one night,

466
00:16:25,413 --> 00:16:27,712
very faint, through the hiss,

467
00:16:27,712 --> 00:16:31,402
two words come back from a city a long way inland.

468
00:16:31,402 --> 00:16:32,735
"Bridge's ours."

469
00:16:33,830 --> 00:16:37,383
On day 386, Vera takes Ansel's lamp

470
00:16:37,383 --> 00:16:39,493
up to the top of the lighthouse,

471
00:16:39,493 --> 00:16:41,945
and lights it, and puts it in the window.

472
00:16:41,945 --> 00:16:43,255
Not the great lamp.

473
00:16:43,255 --> 00:16:44,106
Just a small,

474
00:16:44,106 --> 00:16:47,680
ordinary one, in the window of the room below.

475
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:50,267
"So somebody knows," she says,

476
00:16:50,267 --> 00:16:52,944
"that somebody has seen them."

477
00:16:52,944 --> 00:16:55,827
On day 390, somebody sees it.

478
00:16:55,827 --> 00:16:59,907
It is your turn on watch at the top of the lighthouse,

479
00:16:59,907 --> 00:17:01,242
with Kit, past midnight.

480
00:17:01,242 --> 00:17:03,211
The sea is calm and black.

481
00:17:03,211 --> 00:17:05,020
The causeway is under the water.

482
00:17:05,020 --> 00:17:06,127
Behind you,

483
00:17:06,127 --> 00:17:08,117
the small lamp burns in the window.

484
00:17:08,117 --> 00:17:09,655
And out on the sea,

485
00:17:09,655 --> 00:17:11,446
far away, where there should be

486
00:17:11,446 --> 00:17:13,645
nothing at all, there is a light.

487
00:17:13,645 --> 00:17:14,799
It's moving.

488
00:17:14,799 --> 00:17:15,509
Slowly.

489
00:17:15,509 --> 00:17:17,375
Toward the rock.

490
00:17:17,375 --> 00:17:18,864
Kit grips your sleeve.

491
00:17:18,864 --> 00:17:21,029
You watch it come, for a long time,

492
00:17:21,029 --> 00:17:23,191
until it's close enough to tell that it

493
00:17:23,191 --> 00:17:24,397
is low on the water,

494
00:17:24,397 --> 00:17:27,779
and swinging a little, the way a lamp swings on a boat.

495
00:17:27,779 --> 00:17:29,350
Then it flashes.

496
00:17:29,350 --> 00:17:30,297
Twice.

497
00:17:30,990 --> 00:17:31,336
Hard.

498
00:17:31,336 --> 00:17:32,663
Kit is already running

499
00:17:32,663 --> 00:17:34,740
down the stairs, shouting.

500
00:17:34,740 --> 00:17:36,124
Ruth comes up, and Tam,

501
00:17:36,124 --> 00:17:39,620
and Nora with the flashlight, and all of you stand

502
00:17:39,620 --> 00:17:42,043
at the window, staring out at the dark.

503
00:17:42,352 --> 00:17:44,857
"That's our knock," says Ruth slowly.

504
00:17:44,857 --> 00:17:46,785
"Every boat of ours is tied

505
00:17:46,785 --> 00:17:48,861
up in the harbor," says Tam.

506
00:17:49,251 --> 00:17:50,717
Out on the black water,

507
00:17:50,717 --> 00:17:52,244
the light flashes again.

508
00:17:52,244 --> 00:17:53,265
Twice.

509
00:17:53,265 --> 00:17:53,773
Hard.

510
00:17:53,773 --> 00:17:54,620
And then,

511
00:17:54,620 --> 00:17:58,671
behind it, farther out, a second light comes on.

512
00:17:58,671 --> 00:17:59,811
And a third.

513
00:18:00,186 --> 00:18:01,007
Three hundred and ninety days.

514
00:18:01,007 --> 00:18:03,360
The same orange bandage.

515
00:18:03,718 --> 00:18:05,484
Nora is holding the flashlight.

516
00:18:05,484 --> 00:18:07,551
You are holding the orange bag.

517
00:18:07,909 --> 00:18:09,731
Tomorrow is day 391.

518
00:18:09,731 --> 00:18:12,538
The dead are on an island the sea

519
00:18:12,538 --> 00:18:13,712
won't open for a year,

520
00:18:13,712 --> 00:18:16,287
Bram's gate stands across the causeway,

521
00:18:16,287 --> 00:18:19,661
and a postcard that says Still here is in your bag.

522
00:18:19,661 --> 00:18:21,889
For three hundred and ninety days,

523
00:18:22,248 --> 00:18:24,674
every door you ever had was on land.

524
00:18:24,674 --> 00:18:26,999
Tonight, for the first time,

525
00:18:26,999 --> 00:18:28,741
somebody is knocking on the sea.

526
00:18:28,741 --> 00:18:29,902
Would you have driven

527
00:18:29,902 --> 00:18:31,230
the bus onto the sand?

528
00:18:31,230 --> 00:18:33,338
Who do you think is out on the water?

529
00:18:33,744 --> 00:18:35,066
Tell us in the comments,

530
00:18:35,066 --> 00:18:37,111
and subscribe to Last Safe Door,

531
00:18:37,438 --> 00:18:40,037
so you're here for day 391.
